  "summary": "Bartholomew is named among the Twelve in Luke and among the disciples gathered in Acts. The brief references place him in the apostolic group but offer little individual biography.",
  "historical_context": "Luke 6:12-16 names Bartholomew among the Twelve, and Acts 1:13 includes him in the group gathered in Jerusalem after Jesus's ascension. The cited Matthew passages provide context about the disciples but do not name Bartholomew individually. These texts establish his place in the group, not a detailed account of his life or later ministry.",
