  "literary_context": "Luke 6 lists Bartholomew among the Twelve, and Acts 1 lists him among the disciples gathered after Jesus's ascension. Matthew 4 narrates the calls of Peter, Andrew, James, and John, while Matthew 16 gives Peter the individual response in a scene with the disciples. Those group scenes should not be read as personal statements or actions by Bartholomew.",
  "covenantal_significance": "Bartholomew participates in the move from promise to fulfillment as the gospel goes to the nations.",
